    {
      "id": "CO-ING-8-2026-W36-modal-verbs-adv-001-MASTERY-v7",
      "statement": "**Sentence A:** He must have finished the report. (I'm sure he did it).\n**Sentence B:** He should have finished the report. (He didn't do it, and it's a problem).\n\nWhich sentence expresses **criticism**?",
      "context": "Distinguishing \"must have\" and \"should have\".",
      "options": [
        {
          "letter": "A",
          "text": "Sentence A",
          "is_correct": false,
          "feedback": "Incorrect. This is a deduction."
        },
        {
          "letter": "B",
          "text": "Sentence B",
          "is_correct": true,
          "feedback": "Correct! \"Should have\" implies a missed obligation."
        },
        {
          "letter": "C",
          "text": "Both.",
          "is_correct": false,
          "feedback": "Incorrect."
        },
        {
          "letter": "D",
          "text": "Neither.",
          "is_correct": false,
          "feedback": "Incorrect."
        }
      ],
      "correct_answer": "B",
      "explanation": "Es crucial para un estudiante B1 distinguir entre la deducción (must have) y la crítica o arrepentimiento (should have) en el pasado.\n\n---",
